# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VedMoulya — Web App Environment (example)
# MOB-001 — Mobile Authentication · PROD-02B — server environment boundary
# Copy to `.env.local` (web dev) or bake into the build (mobile static export).
#
# WHERE SERVER-SIDE VALUES COME FROM (read this before adding a variable)
#   • The repository's authoritative development values live in the ROOT
#     `.env.local` (database URLs, AI keys, JWT secret, OAuth credentials, …).
#     The web app runs the API gateway INSIDE the Next.js server process, and
#     `apps/web/next.config.ts` + `apps/web/src/lib/server-env.ts` load the root
#     file in development/test, so `npm run dev` sees the SAME values as
#     `npm run preflight` / `bash scripts/startup.sh` / `npm run doctor`.
#   • This file (`apps/web/.env.local`) is for app-local overrides ONLY. Next.js
#     loads it FIRST, and it wins over the root file for the keys it defines.
#   • Production/staging load NEITHER file — the platform environment is the
#     only source (see docs/ops/DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md).
#   • Never expose a server secret through a NEXT_PUBLIC_* name: those are
#     inlined into the browser bundle. Keep every secret server-side.
#     `findLeakedPublicSecrets()` (server-env.ts) reports violations by NAME.
#
# DO NOT copy the root backend configuration here. Duplicating AI keys,
# DATABASE_URL or AUTH_JWT_SECRET into this file creates two sources of truth
# that drift silently — the exact defect this boundary removes.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# tRPC gateway URL. Web: leave unset (same-origin `/api/trpc`). Mobile static
# export (Capacitor): set to the deployed server, e.g. https://api.example.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_URL=

# Identity Service REST API base URL. Web: leave unset (same origin — the
# Next.js app mounts the auth routes at /api/v1/identity/auth). Mobile: set to
# the deployed server, e.g. https://api.example.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_IDENTITY_URL=

# Google OAuth redirect URI — MUST match the identity service's
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI and the redirect URI registered in the Google Cloud
# Console for the OAuth client. Leave unset to default to
# <origin>/oauth2redirect (https://localhost/oauth2redirect inside the
# Capacitor WebView).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=

# Set true to enable mock/dev shortcuts (future) — not implemented yet.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_MOCK=false

# ── App-local overrides (ONLY when a web-specific value must differ) ────────
# Google OAuth is the one credential pair that legitimately lives here when the
# Next.js dev origin differs from the backend's; everything else belongs in the
# root file.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/v1/identity/auth/google/callback

